  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "The number of one-one functions <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>a</mi></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>b</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>d</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;is _____",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "31",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>a</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>c</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>b</mi></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>d</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>Using fundamental principle of counting,</p><p>when&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>c</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>a</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>then</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>b</mi></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>d</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;has&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math>&nbsp;choices,</p><p>Similarly when&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>c</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>a</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>then</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>b</mi></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>d</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;has&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;choices.</p><p>Counting like this we get the total number of one-one function as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>31</mn></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
